                <pb facs="0817" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/248: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Coolidge to President Guggiari</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                        1928</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have received Your Excellency’s telegram of December 9 in relation to the
                    regrettable conflict that has taken place between Paraguay and Bolivia and, in
                    thanking Your Excellency for advising me regarding this matter, I desire to
                    express the most fervent hope that the difficulty between your country and
                    Bolivia will soon be composed to the entire satisfaction of both parties.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Calvin Coolidge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
